Z||000006||FOCONE||06-18-2001||11:33 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><B>Who won the ratty Fiero?<BR>And why did the 85 class get cut down to one?<BR>There were at least two 85's there that I saw, and the ballot had 1st and 2nd.<P>Just wonderin'<P>Steve</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Steve,<P>It was explained to all at the show AND dinner why that was cut down. If you have a question call or email me! I and really do not like your accusations of how the count is done or how voting is done!  As you know from the past shows the ballots are available for inspection by any one for, 180 days after any show.<BR>No ratty trophy was not given out.<P>||||reg||4
Z||000007||chester||06-18-2001||12:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FOCONE:<BR><B> <BR>Steve,<P>It was explained to all at the show AND dinner why that was cut down. If you have a question call or email me! I and really do not like your accusations of how the count is done or how voting is done!  As you know from the past shows the ballots are available for inspection by any one for, 180 days after any show.<BR>No ratty trophy was not given out.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well the fact that the 85 class was cut down is news to me.  Also NORMALLY if people do not open the bonnets they get DQ'ed?  Nobody is accusing you of anything. All that was done is a question was asked and you took it as an accusation?  Also a lot of people were asking me why I was not in the decal/paint comp.  No big deal but that was a question brought to me by many at the show. BTW why put a "RATTY" fiero award on the ballot if you do not intend on awarding it?  Just another question, not and accusation. I know for a fact that I did vote for the "ratty" class so there was someone to give it to. We did enjoy the show and want to thank all that voted for me!  Couldn't have done it without you folks!!!<P>Rob D.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000008||Jaygee79||06-18-2001||02:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FOCONE:<BR><B> <BR>Steve,<P>It was explained to all at the show AND dinner why that was cut down. If you have a question call or email me! I and really do not like your accusations of how the count is done or how voting is done!  As you know from the past shows the ballots are available for inspection by any one for, 180 days after any show.<BR>No ratty trophy was not given out.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Geez you need to chill out.  I heard it explained at the dinner but NOT at the show.  If someone did explain then they should've talked louder because I don't think anyone heard.  And I don't remember anything being said about why only 1 award for 85 was given out.  You need to learn the difference between an accusation and a question.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||88CoupeV6||06-18-2001||05:17 PM||||I have a few pics of some cool cars at the show in my Photopoint album. Click under my Sig to see them.<P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000010||FOCONE||06-18-2001||07:28 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaygee79:<BR><B> Geez you need to chill out.  I heard it explained at the dinner but NOT at the show.  If someone did explain then they should've talked louder because I don't think anyone heard.  And I don't remember anything being said about why only 1 award for 85 was given out.  You need to learn the difference between an accusation and a question.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>If you had a car in the show you were told then, along with it listed in print.||||reg||4
Z||000011||Fiero5||06-18-2001||09:33 PM||||"If you had a car in the show you were told then, along with it listed in print"<P>None of my family were told that when we arrived, and that is 4 Fieros if anyone is counting. The ballots had a 1st and 2nd for the 85 class and also had a ratty Fiero class. The 85 class had one winner, of which is arguable that it should not have qualified due to the lids being down. My son had more than a few people come over while he was cleaning his Fiero and tell him that to be eligeable for a trophy, he had to have his lids up during voting. So he quickly raised them up.<P>I don't like being told that I am accusing anyone, when all I am doing is asking a few very valid questions. Some in fact that I am passing on from others who obviously knew that this is the kind of reaction they might get. What does that tell you?<BR>And I still haven't seen a valid reason for why the 85 class didn't have more than one trophy, as it had more than one 85 in the class. Hello?? Add to that a valid reason why there was no ratty Fiero winner too.<P>Still wonderin'<P>Steve ||||reg||5
Z||000012||Old Lar||06-18-2001||09:33 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Convert.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/IndyConvertible.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ModRow.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Stocks.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/5LV8.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Tina.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000013||grgoyl86||06-18-2001||09:44 PM||||Hi folks.<P>Just curious. How many Fieros were in attendance overall? Looks like beautiful weather on the pictures.<P>Bob||||reg||3
Z||000014||Fiero2||06-18-2001||09:59 PM||||"Well the fact that the 85 class was cut down is news to me. Also NORMALLY if people do not open the bonnets they get DQ'ed? Nobody is accusing you of anything. All that was done is a question was asked and you took it as an accusation? Also a lot of people were asking me why I was not in the decal/paint comp. No big deal but that was a question brought to me by many at the show. BTW why put a "RATTY" fiero award on the ballot if you do not intend on awarding it? Just another question, not and accusation. I know for a fact that I did vote for the "ratty" class so there was someone to give it to. We did enjoy the show and want to thank all that voted for me! Couldn't have done it without you folks!!!<P> Rob D."<P>We got a few e-mails asking us why a T-Top model won 100% original. Can a T-Top Fiero  qualify for 100% original? I guess we always thought that was a dealer option, not factory so not original.<BR>Can anyone answer this?<P>Thanks<P>Marian <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Marians_sig_1.jpg">  <BR>I LOVE my Fiero!!!||||reg||5
Z||000015||Jaygee79||06-18-2001||10:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FOCONE:<BR><B> <BR>If you had a car in the show you were told then, along with it listed in print.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I was talking about the Rattiest Fiero award.<P>------------------<BR>Jaime<BR>84SE red<BR>AOL IM: Jaygee79<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/jaygee79/index.html" TARGET=_blank>Jaygee79's Web Page</A><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pooheey1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000016||mrfiero||06-19-2001||12:12 AM||||An '88 Fiero with the RPO code CJB can be considered original (that's the code for the T-Tops).  They were not dealer ordered......when you ordered your Fiero in '88 you could check the T-Top box on the order blank, so it is in fact a factory ordered option.  True, they were not fitted with T-Tops at the factory, but it is considered original equipment if it has the CJB code.<P>Any other year or any '88 Fiero without the CJB code is not original.  In that case I too would have a grudge against it winning a stock original class.<P>I hope this clarifies things.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||fyerstarter||06-19-2001||06:42 AM||||Ummm...you guys sound like a couple of anal yuppies arguing over a golf game. Last time I checked car shows were about having fun! and not winning, and certainly not complaining about minor details in judging. If you were to win you would want to win because you car ****ING KICKS ASS! and blew the judges out of their seat, not by some technicality such as t-tops not matching codes and **** , right?||||reg||1
Z||000018||Fiero5||06-19-2001||08:45 AM||||Well, that answers one question with the T-Tops anyway. How tough was that?<BR>As for any of us sounding like anal yuppies, all a few of us did was ask a few questions. As usual, it probably will and allready is starting to get blown all out of proportion.<BR>I love it when people try to hide behind "you should go for the fun" when a question like this comes up. Which in fact is always a great way to try and sweep controversy under the rug. Nice try though.<P>Fact: There were at least 2 85's at the show, but only one trophy awarded. If yours was the 85 that got snubbed, especially when you know you got votes you wouldn't be saying what you are now. <BR>Fact: There was a Ratty Fiero class and votes were made for that class by the participants, yet no award was given. Again, if you had votes given you would want to know also I bet. Well, there are some who want to know.<P>They were a few simple questions that those who should have answered and moved on chose not to. So now it is starting to turn into something it shouldn't have.<P>At this point I don't realy care anymore. It's Focones show and they will do whatever it is they do for their show. people can either except that or not. If they have a problem with how they see it was handled, don't bug me or my family or grumble to anyone else for that matter about it. Just decide to go or not, and then except what happens and move on. <P>Steve Kelley||||reg||7
Z||000019||Indyellowgt||06-19-2001||09:26 AM||||OK,folks....lets clear the air here a little.<BR>My 85GT took first place.When I arrived to the fair ground that morning,I parked the 85,then had to leave to get my INDY car.When I came back,after I parked the Indy,I had to register,pay my dues,etc..etc..Then I opened the bonnets on my 85 GT.<BR>I worked very hard to get my cars to the show,and I feel my 85 was a great example.I had detailed under BOTH hoods,as well as the paint and interior.<BR>So...If you did not see the hood(s) open on my white 85 GT at first,I did have them open at 11am(plenty of time for voters).<BR>I really,really enjoy my Fieros,and ALL Fiero shows.But I just can't figure *why* there is always trouble in the aftermath...<BR>Everyone says they love Fieros..,and enjoys them,I know I do. I really did not want to weigh in this topoic,but it pretty much involves me...If any one at the show feels that my 85 GT was not suitable for a trophy over Steve's son's yellow/purple 85 GT,I'm open to critisism,Really...<BR>If you want the trophy that bad,Get me your address,I'll mail it to you.<BR>That is not why I go to all the shows....<P>Hope to see you all at Bob Parkers Kick Hill in July.<P>-Mark Webber.||||reg||1
Z||000020||Fiero5||06-19-2001||05:36 PM||||Mark, no one said your 85 was not deserving of a trophy. The only question that some brought up was that they didn't think your lids were up. Since they apparently were, there shouldn't be anything more to say on it taking a trophy.  Let me be the first to opologize if any of my statements were misunderstood on your 85 winning. I didn't see your lids up, but I wasn't watching your Fiero every minute either. My question has always been why the 85 class had a 1st and 2nd place, and then at the last minute dropped to just a 1st place only. I didn't think much about it until we received a few e-mails the next day asking why only one 85 took a trophy. The first e-mails I got I still didn't even know who the winners were. When I finally found the list posted, I had no idea why only one place was awarded, so I asked. After seing that a ratty award was never given out, I asked why on that also.<P>Unfortunately it has gotten a bit blown out of proportion since those questions were first asked. I am sure I haven't helped any in my continuing to ask for a reason why.<P>My son said all day and after the show, that he figured you for first, so don't let anything that has been said make you feel like your awesome 85 didn't deserve it. My son was told by a bunch of people that they voted for his Fiero in the 85, so he figured he had a shot at second place. The question that some people have, including myself is, why the decision at the last minute to eliminate the 2nd place award in the 85 class, and the ratty one as well for that matter? We are not complaining, we are just asking. How else do you get an answer other than by asking?<P>If anyone wants to try and say that any member of the Kelley family is upset because one of us didn't win a trophy at OOB this year, they couldn't be more further from the truth. My family and I have always gone for the fun. Everyone who knows us will back up the fact that we do NOT go to win an award.<BR>We love to drive to a show, park the Fiero(s), clean them up and then go yack with everyone. We have been going to shows for years, and have never been upset about not placing. We have even taken our Fieros to car shows where we knew we would be put up against Corvettes and the like. We knew we wouldn't place there, but the reason we went was to go and have fun. We wanted others to see our little cars and get it a little deserved exposure. We didn't get any awards, but we got something worth alot more. New freinds and alot of exposure to our little Fieros. Exposure to other car people who may not have seen one in a show otherwise. Many of the shows we go to look at us funny when we arrive in a "Fiero". But once we are there and the show people see the interest in our Fieros, they have a different opinion of the Fiero at a muscle or classic car show afterwards. That is what makes it fun.<BR>Spindles is a great example. The first year we went was with my white 84. What strange looks we got when we showed up. The following year Renee' Dabrowski worked with us to get our very own Fiero class added at Spindles. Bob Parker of Kick Hill Farms sponsored the trophies and we really showed them with a great turnout and the largest trophies that club has ever seen at their show. The trophies were four times the size of their show trophies and twice the size of their best of show! My family and I worked with Renee' to get the class added. I then got the class sponsored thanks to Bob Parker and was able to get some awesome trophies made at the last minute. You know what? None of my family placed at the show. That wasn't why we did it, and we couldn't have been happier for those who did win. It took alot of effort, but the outcome was well worth every minute we spent getting it done. The Lebanon NH show is another example, and on and on.<P>The only issue people have here is that there were votes given for at least two Fieros in the 85 class that had a 1st and 2nd on the ballot, and yet only one trophy was given out. Why? Add the missing Ratty award one to this, and you can't blame people for wondering what happened.<P>Steve||||reg||7
Z||000021||FOCONE||06-19-2001||05:55 PM||||Steve,<P>A recount for the 3 cars in the 85 class<BR>to see who would have taken 2nd if it was not removed 2 WEEKS BEFORE THE SHOW.<BR>A phone call will be made to Chris with the<BR>final outcome in that class.<P>tim||||reg||1
Z||000022||FOCONE||06-19-2001||08:25 PM||||Steve,<P>This is it!  If you wish to see the ballots call me to set up a time to look them over. I will not be responding<BR>to any of your many  e-mails to F.O.C.O.N.E..  The other club officers have answered your questions many times over.  As to the Ratty Fiero Award the person that won it did not wish to be named. I have listed the car numbers below, with a “XX” in that persons place. As a result of your actions and the fact that the person that won, was so mortified over winning it, we will no longer have that award at our shows.<BR>We will also no longer have the best paint or decals award, remember this was started for one of your cars<BR>at the 99 show, and if remember correctly YOU WON IT! Then I did my car and started to win  that award.<P>Finial results!<P>As is, nothing has changed from the first time they had been counted.  Some did not turn in there<BR>ballots and some did not vote for the Ratty Fiero.<P>#<BR>14		2  votes<BR>xx		11 votes<BR>18		1 vote	<BR>15		9 votes<BR>23		1 vote<BR>31		1 vote	<BR>16		1 vote<BR>19		1 vote<BR>2 votes that had been cast that could not be clearly read, one looks like #75or #35 and the other looks like #13 or #18  it is stated in the rules, if it can’t be read, it will not count.<P>1985 class<P>20		15 votes     Mark<BR>32		8 votes       Tina<BR>14		7 votes	    Steven<P>ALSO, DON’T YOU EVER QUESTION MY WIFE’S INTEGRITY OR <BR>THE CLUB AND IT’S OFFICERS FOR THAT MATTER.  I WOULD HAVE TO SAY WE ARE ALL DUE AN APOLOGY FOR THE STATEMENTS YOU MADE IN YOUR EMAILS TO F.O.C.O.N.E.  IT WAS ALL OK WHEN YOU ARE WINNING, BUT THE SECOND YOU DO NOT, LOOK OUT.  WHO WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE COUNT THE VOTES???????? THAT IS WHY THE BALLOTS ARE LEFT OPEN TO INSPECTION, TO ALL!  SINCE THE FIRST SHOW IN 1996 NO ONE HAS EVER SAID BOO ABOUT WHO COUNTS THEM, AND IF YOU LOOK BACK THIS IS THE FIRST TIME I HAVE EVER PLACED SO HIGH AT ONE OF OUR SHOWS PERIOD,<BR>END OF STORY!  THIS WAS ONE OF THE BEST SHOWS EVER, KEEP IT THAT WAY!<P>TIM<P>||||reg||4
Z||000023||Jaygee79||06-19-2001||10:56 PM||||OK obviously you 2 have a beef with each other.  Can't you keep it in email instead of taking up valuable space here?  If the problems were in email then keep it there.  Don't take it public.  JMHO.||||reg||1
Z||000024||FOCONE||06-19-2001||11:17 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jaygee79:<BR><B>OK obviously you 2 have a beef with each other.  Can't you keep it in email instead of taking up valuable space here?  If the problems were in email then keep it there.  Don't take it public.  JMHO.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>We don't have a problem, Steve has a problem!<BR>He is the one that took it public!<BR>End of story!<BR>tim<P>||||reg||4
Z||000025||Fiero5||06-20-2001||12:50 AM||||Well, that was an interesting read.<BR>Let me be allowed my response to these “accusations” if I may. It's kinda long, so those who have had enough just hit your back button.<P>Tim wrote: “I will not be responding<BR>to any of your many e-mails to F.O.C.O.N.E..”<P>Tim you never responded to my e-mails to Focone. I tried to keep it off list, but all I kept getting was your officers responding with everything but the answers to the few questions I asked. I ended up being accused of everything short of the JFK assasination. Your officers also asked that those who e-mailed me off list some of the questions to please step forward so they can help explain it to them directly. Now everyone can see why they didn’t want to do that in the first place, and asked me to ask instead. They knew I had the balls to ask and they were right. I can take the heat, as I usually know when to open my mouth and when not to. I am not always 100% in getting it right, but I think in this case the forum can make their own decisions as if it was justified. Though they may be getting a bit sick of the arguing at this point I am sure.<P>“The other club officers have answered your questions many times over.”<P>Like I just said, they didn’t. I would like to point out that I did keep it off list until it was apparent I wasn’t getting anywhere that way except getting slammed.<P>“As to the Ratty Fiero Award the person that won it did not wish to be named. &gt; As a result of your actions and the fact that the person that won, was so mortified over winning it, we will no longer have that award at our shows.”<P>Let me state a few facts here. The Ratty Fiero actually came out of the Merrimack Bud Brewery show last year from an incident that happened between a few people. A few Pride members decided to run with it after the fact as a fun joke, and even a “Proud Member of the Ratty Fiero Club” T-Shirt came out of it. Then low and behold not soon after you decide to take it and put it in your Focone shows. Now you are trying to say that thanks to “my” actions? <P>“We will also no longer have the best paint or decals award”<BR>Why? Are you saying that because you seem to always win that one, you are going to take it out. Seriously, why are you making that decision?  As I stated to some of your officers earlier, I would think that after winning so many times in a row, maybe take that particular car out of the class and let someone else have a chance. I just saw in one of the recent neswsletters that one Fiero that had won a particular award so many times in row, was kept out of that particular  class this year. It still ended up winning something like the peoples choice but you get the idea. <P>“remember this (the paint and decal award) was started for one of your cars<BR>at the 99 show, and if remember correctly YOU WON IT! Then I did my car and started to win that award.”<P>Well, once again you are completely wrong. It was created for Dennis’s white w/blue stripes T-Top GT in 99 for the fall show, that you had actually seen a few weeks earlier before the show. Though you told everyone at the show during awards time that back when you first saw it, it was actually a beautiful blue. You said you loved his paint job so much you created the paint and decal award just for him then.<P>“1985 class<BR>20 15 votes Mark<BR>32 8 votes Tina<BR>14 7 votes Steven”<P>So I assume then that Tina is due a 2nd place trophy? Congrats Tina.<P>“ALSO, DON’T YOU EVER QUESTION MY WIFE’S INTEGRITY”<P>I NEVER did Tim, so don’t accuse me of saying something I never said! What I said was that any close relative of a show participant shouldn’t be counting ballots. It can create an air of question.<P>“OR THE CLUB AND IT’S OFFICERS FOR THAT MATTER.”<BR>Your club officers after sending me a few useless e-mails then took it upon themselves to attack me like ravaged dogs, so anything I said to them after was deserved. <P>“I WOULD HAVE TO SAY WE ARE ALL DUE AN APOLOGY FOR THE STATEMENTS YOU MADE IN YOUR EMAILS TO F.O.C.O.N.E.”<P>Actually, I believe that it is the opposit here. After all the crap I have taken in the last day or so over asking two simple questions, which you all decided to ignore and instead accuse and finger point at me I think I am owed a few at least. Why did I get slammed? For daring to question why the 85 class had only one trophy awarded, etc . Say nothing of all your incorrect statements here.<BR>For example, here is an e-mail I just received from someone in the Fiero community who has been following this:<BR>“I have a question, and I thought<BR>I would ask you. If I read that right, in Tim's early reply he said it was<BR>announced at the show that there would be only one trophy for the class.<BR>Right? Now, in the last reply or two, he mentioned that it was announced two<BR>weeks earlier. Did I read that right?”<P>Interesting isn’t it?<P>“IT WAS ALL OK WHEN YOU ARE WINNING, BUT THE SECOND YOU DO NOT, LOOK OUT.”<P>This statement is just laughable. When your officers state that they go for the fun and not to win, we are all supposed to believe them. But when I say the exact same thing and have many friends who can back it up 100%, I am instead accused of being upset for not winning. Guess what Tim, I had an 86 that day, remember? I never questioned not winning in my class. I have won once at one of your shows over the years, of which you end up getting it wrong twice! And I have never complained as like I have said, I go for the fun.<P>“WHO WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE COUNT THE VOTES????????”<P>I told your officers, one at a time many times that it should be someone who doesn’t have anyone close to them tied to the show. An unbiased person. Chris responded to that by saying it was OK for your wife to count the ballots, as she is the most honest person he knows. I responded that it didn’t matter if she is the most honest person next to GOD, she is your wife and you had multiple cars in the show (3 I think) and so that should automatically disqualify her from counting ballots.<BR>I wasn’t insulting her, I was only stated how it is supposed to be done.  <P>“THAT IS WHY THE BALLOTS ARE LEFT OPEN TO INSPECTION, TO ALL!”<P>If I was little closer than 3 plus hours away, I might take you up on that. <P>“SINCE THE FIRST SHOW IN 1996 NO ONE HAS EVER SAID BOO ABOUT WHO COUNTS THEM”<P>Actually that is also not true. There were some who grumbled at the ballot counting at every Focone show I have been to.  I have also heard from some who used to go to Focone shows even before I have neen going that these “questions” have been common place even back then. And you know the people I am talking about Tim. When I heard these at the first few Focone shows I was at, I simply blew it off as I was new and figured that you would probably always have some who would complain about such things. In fact, I have received a few e-mails just awhile ago who read your response here and sent me e-mails. One said they were at the Rutland show last fall. They stated that they and some others were surprised to see you, Chris and another person at the Rutland show last year under the small tent counting some of the ballots. The other said a similar statement.<P>“AND IF YOU LOOK BACK THIS IS THE FIRST TIME I HAVE EVER PLACED SO HIGH AT ONE OF OUR SHOWS PERIOD,”<P>Again not entirely true. In fact you admit to winning the Best of paint and Decal award many times. Since that was the only Fiero you entered at the time, it is true that was possibly as high as you could get. Having multiple cars at OOB this year, you got many more awards and placed higher in some.<P>“END OF STORY! THIS WAS ONE OF THE BEST SHOWS EVER,”<P>Yes, I agree that this was much better than last years much smaller turnout. I give you congrats at least for such a good turnout.<P>“KEEP IT THAT WAY!”<BR>Well, that is up to you now Tim, isn’t it?||||reg||9
Z||000026||FOCONE||06-20-2001||04:19 AM||||So did your questions get answered?<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fiero5:<BR><B>Well, that was an interesting read.<BR>Let me be allowed my response to these “accusations” if I may. It's kinda long, so those who have had enough just hit your back button.<P>Tim wrote: “I will not be responding<BR>to any of your many e-mails to F.O.C.O.N.E..”<P>Tim you never responded to my e-mails to Focone. I tried to keep it off list, but all I kept getting was your officers responding with everything but the answers to the few questions I asked. I ended up being accused of everything short of the JFK assasination. Your officers also asked that those who e-mailed me off list some of the questions to please step forward so they can help explain it to them directly. Now everyone can see why they didn’t want to do that in the first place, and asked me to ask instead. They knew I had the balls to ask and they were right. I can take the heat, as I usually know when to open my mouth and when not to. I am not always 100% in getting it right, but I think in this case the forum can make their own decisions as if it was justified. Though they may be getting a bit sick of the arguing at this point I am sure.<P>“The other club officers have answered your questions many times over.”<P>Like I just said, they didn’t. I would like to point out that I did keep it off list until it was apparent I wasn’t getting anywhere that way except getting slammed.<P>“As to the Ratty Fiero Award the person that won it did not wish to be named. &gt; As a result of your actions and the fact that the person that won, was so mortified over winning it, we will no longer have that award at our shows.”<P>Let me state a few facts here. The Ratty Fiero actually came out of the Merrimack Bud Brewery show last year from an incident that happened between a few people. A few Pride members decided to run with it after the fact as a fun joke, and even a “Proud Member of the Ratty Fiero Club” T-Shirt came out of it. Then low and behold not soon after you decide to take it and put it in your Focone shows. Now you are trying to say that thanks to “my” actions? <P>“We will also no longer have the best paint or decals award”<BR>Why? Are you saying that because you seem to always win that one, you are going to take it out. Seriously, why are you making that decision?  As I stated to some of your officers earlier, I would think that after winning so many times in a row, maybe take that particular car out of the class and let someone else have a chance. I just saw in one of the recent neswsletters that one Fiero that had won a particular award so many times in row, was kept out of that particular  class this year. It still ended up winning something like the peoples choice but you get the idea. <P>“remember this (the paint and decal award) was started for one of your cars<BR>at the 99 show, and if remember correctly YOU WON IT! Then I did my car and started to win that award.”<P>Well, once again you are completely wrong. It was created for Dennis’s white w/blue stripes T-Top GT in 99 for the fall show, that you had actually seen a few weeks earlier before the show. Though you told everyone at the show during awards time that back when you first saw it, it was actually a beautiful blue. You said you loved his paint job so much you created the paint and decal award just for him then.<P>“1985 class<BR>20 15 votes Mark<BR>32 8 votes Tina<BR>14 7 votes Steven”<P>So I assume then that Tina is due a 2nd place trophy? Congrats Tina.<P>“ALSO, DON’T YOU EVER QUESTION MY WIFE’S INTEGRITY”<P>I NEVER did Tim, so don’t accuse me of saying something I never said! What I said was that any close relative of a show participant shouldn’t be counting ballots. It can create an air of question.<P>“OR THE CLUB AND IT’S OFFICERS FOR THAT MATTER.”<BR>Your club officers after sending me a few useless e-mails then took it upon themselves to attack me like ravaged dogs, so anything I said to them after was deserved. <P>“I WOULD HAVE TO SAY WE ARE ALL DUE AN APOLOGY FOR THE STATEMENTS YOU MADE IN YOUR EMAILS TO F.O.C.O.N.E.”<P>Actually, I believe that it is the opposit here. After all the crap I have taken in the last day or so over asking two simple questions, which you all decided to ignore and instead accuse and finger point at me I think I am owed a few at least. Why did I get slammed? For daring to question why the 85 class had only one trophy awarded, etc . Say nothing of all your incorrect statements here.<BR>For example, here is an e-mail I just received from someone in the Fiero community who has been following this:<BR>“I have a question, and I thought<BR>I would ask you. If I read that right, in Tim's early reply he said it was<BR>announced at the show that there would be only one trophy for the class.<BR>Right? Now, in the last reply or two, he mentioned that it was announced two<BR>weeks earlier. Did I read that right?”<P>Interesting isn’t it?<P>“IT WAS ALL OK WHEN YOU ARE WINNING, BUT THE SECOND YOU DO NOT, LOOK OUT.”<P>This statement is just laughable. When your officers state that they go for the fun and not to win, we are all supposed to believe them. But when I say the exact same thing and have many friends who can back it up 100%, I am instead accused of being upset for not winning. Guess what Tim, I had an 86 that day, remember? I never questioned not winning in my class. I have won once at one of your shows over the years, of which you end up getting it wrong twice! And I have never complained as like I have said, I go for the fun.<P>“WHO WOULD YOU LIKE TO SEE COUNT THE VOTES????????”<P>I told your officers, one at a time many times that it should be someone who doesn’t have anyone close to them tied to the show. An unbiased person. Chris responded to that by saying it was OK for your wife to count the ballots, as she is the most honest person he knows. I responded that it didn’t matter if she is the most honest person next to GOD, she is your wife and you had multiple cars in the show (3 I think) and so that should automatically disqualify her from counting ballots.<BR>I wasn’t insulting her, I was only stated how it is supposed to be done.  <P>“THAT IS WHY THE BALLOTS ARE LEFT OPEN TO INSPECTION, TO ALL!”<P>If I was little closer than 3 plus hours away, I might take you up on that. <P>“SINCE THE FIRST SHOW IN 1996 NO ONE HAS EVER SAID BOO ABOUT WHO COUNTS THEM”<P>Actually that is also not true. There were some who grumbled at the ballot counting at every Focone show I have been to.  I have also heard from some who used to go to Focone shows even before I have neen going that these “questions” have been common place even back then. And you know the people I am talking about Tim. When I heard these at the first few Focone shows I was at, I simply blew it off as I was new and figured that you would probably always have some who would complain about such things. In fact, I have received a few e-mails just awhile ago who read your response here and sent me e-mails. One said they were at the Rutland show last fall. They stated that they and some others were surprised to see you, Chris and another person at the Rutland show last year under the small tent counting some of the ballots. The other said a similar statement.<P>“AND IF YOU LOOK BACK THIS IS THE FIRST TIME I HAVE EVER PLACED SO HIGH AT ONE OF OUR SHOWS PERIOD,”<P>Again not entirely true. In fact you admit to winning the Best of paint and Decal award many times. Since that was the only Fiero you entered at the time, it is true that was possibly as high as you could get. Having multiple cars at OOB this year, you got many more awards and placed higher in some.<P>“END OF STORY! THIS WAS ONE OF THE BEST SHOWS EVER,”<P>Yes, I agree that this was much better than last years much smaller turnout. I give you congrats at least for such a good turnout.<P>“KEEP IT THAT WAY!”<BR>Well, that is up to you now Tim, isn’t it?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><p>[This message has been edited by FOCONE (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||5
Z||000027||FOCONE||06-20-2001||07:24 AM||||Steve,<P>I will say this again.<P>All of your questions have been answered already OFF LIST.  Remember when you E-mailed focone@focone.org and asked the same questions over and over again.<P>Below is just a sample of the E-mails that you sent us and one of our replies.<P>I seem to remember hearing that you were not happy at another NON FOCONE car show were you did not win anything.<P>Enjoy rereading.  We do have more.<P>Chris Schaefer<P><BR>Subject:Re: [Fwd: An FYI and a personal question]<BR>   Date:Mon, 18 Jun 2001 16:44:26 -0400<BR>   From:Chris Schaefer &lt;chris.schaefer@focone.org&gt;<BR>     To:steve_kelley@hhs.dresden.k12.nh.us<BR>     CC:focone@focone.org<P>Steve,<P>Thank you, but I must say that without everyone’s attendance there would be<BR>no showing.  So I must say thank you to you and your family and to everyone<BR>else who was there.<P>We are currently looking into creating new show classes for our fall show.<BR>But as Tim mentioned the evening of the show, those who pre-register<BR>dictate what classes we can have.  Pre-registration is vital so we don’t<BR>waste money on buy trophies for cars that just don’t show.<P>Your idea for the paint/decal class is also a good idea.  We will take that<BR>into consideration when we create or add new car classes.<P>With regards to how people prefer to show their cars, open or closed, we do<BR>not want to be so stringent as to how people should prepare their cars.<BR>Personal, if there are two cars in a class with both being rather equal in<BR>external appearance but one is open while the other is closed, I vote for<BR>the open car.  That is just my personal feelings which may not agree with<BR>others.<P>The 84 and 85 classes have always been the hardest to plan for.  As you may<BR>remember from attending some of our other shows in the past, the 84 and 85<BR>classes don’t usually have more than 1 or 2 cars.  This was true again with<BR>this past shows pre-registrations.  So at the last minute we moved the<BR>trophies that were set aside for the 2nd places for the 84 and 85’s to the<BR>modified classes.  Which we also the morning of the show added 2 more for a<BR>total of 6 places for the modifieds (due to a total of 13+ cars in that<BR>class).  We all strive to do our best so everyone will be happy and have a<BR>good time.<P>BTW, please pass along to those who have contacted you that they are more<BR>than welcome to contact us with their questions.  This would be best as we<BR>can all be assured accurate information between those who have<BR>questions/complains and ourselves.<P>Let me try to address some of your questions.<P>#1.  I believe that 2 paragraphs above should answer this one.<P>#2.  The main members of FOCONE are my self, Tim Perrigo, Joe Becker, Joe<BR>Wynman and Jim Lund.  None of us had any contact with the ballots until<BR>after the awards were handed out.  Tim’s wife Joyce, who doesn’t even know<BR>who’s car has which number, has always counted up the ballots.  Joyce makes<BR>sure than no one gets near the ballots for security reasons.<P>#3. Tim tries to make sure that as many people as possible are able to go<BR>home with an award.  There are certain classes that are more popular than<BR>others.  It is these classes that Tim has to work so hard at.  That is why<BR>pre-registration is so important.  Frankly, Tim is still shocked that his<BR>T-top car beat Cliff Knights Yellow GT just because Yellow is his favorite<BR>color.<P>Anyhow, I am glad that you had a good time.  It is always good to see so<BR>many people enjoying themselves with the cars they like so much.  After<BR>all, that is what these shows are all about.<P>I asked Tim about your show registration.  You mailed your show<BR>registration to Tim (post marked May 23rd) and he received it May 26th.<BR>The show pre-registration and membership special expired on April 31st.<BR>There were only a total of 5 people who qualified for the poster.<BR>Unfortunately, your registration was mailed after the special had expired.<P>As for the club magazine, the 3rd quarter issue is on schedule and will be<BR>mailed the end of July to the beginning of August.  Either just before or<BR>just after the FOCOA Nationals.<P>Now it is time for me to return to work.<P>Have a good day,<P>Chris<P>At 12:48 PM 6/18/01 -0400, you wrote:<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;Hi there<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;Well, let me first start off by saying congrats on a such a huge turnout.<BR>&gt;It was nice to see so many Fieros, especially from last year. It seems<BR>&gt;that Fieros are getting more popular than ever, and the numbers are<BR>&gt;growing at shows.<BR>&gt;Chris mentioned doing another class next year that split up the mods as it<BR>&gt;was such a huge line in that class. It's too bad you guys couldn't have<BR>&gt;made a quick second mod class this year, but I am sure with the trophies<BR>&gt;allready being done and so forth that wouldn't have worked well. I also<BR>&gt;think that the paint/decal class should be split up, as a car with a<BR>&gt;beautiful extra sweet paint job shouldn't be beat by one with a lot of<BR>&gt;decals and vice versa. They should be seperate in my opinion and others<BR>&gt;have stated the same. Just a thought for next year.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;I was wondering why the 84 and 85 class had only 1st and 2nd, and that in<BR>&gt;both those classes 2nd was apparently eliminated at the last minute? I<BR>&gt;realize that there was only 84 I think, the Indy. There were however at<BR>&gt;least two 85's, so that seemed a bit strange to many including myself.<BR>&gt;I also have recieved a few e-mails in the last few hours asking my opinion<BR>&gt;of the winners list. I thought this a bit odd as I have nothing to do with<BR>&gt;judging (other than my one judging slip I filled out) or the counting of<BR>&gt;ballots, etc. One person (all who asked to remain anonimous) asked why my<BR>&gt;son didn't win in the 85 class. I answered that apparently there was only<BR>&gt;a 1st place, and they said that the 85 that won shouldn't have because it<BR>&gt;didn't have the lids raised which should have in effect disqualified it? I<BR>&gt;thought that was interesting, so I asked this on a Pennocks post then<BR>&gt;also. If that is true, it would explain a few of the new grumblings I am<BR>&gt;getting now. I don't know why my family seems to be the ones who get the<BR>&gt;grumblings, though one person who just e-mailed me said they did so<BR>&gt;because we have so many Fieros and seem to be "in touch" with the local<BR>&gt;clubs.<BR>&gt;Since I know how you felt about the last grumbling that went around, I<BR>&gt;thought I would give you an FYI.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;There seems to be three specific grumblings that I am hearing/getting<BR>&gt;e-mail on at this point:<BR>&gt;1) Why did the 85 class that had at least two Fieros have only one trophy? <BR>&gt;I couldn't answer this one as I was wondering the same thing myself. I am<BR>&gt;also interested in the answer to this as my son was one of the 85's, and<BR>&gt;he had his 85 Fiero on "full" display.<BR>&gt;2) Why did the main members of the club (all who won at least one trophy)<BR>&gt;have such a heavy hand in the ballot counting?<BR>&gt;I couldn't anwser this one either as I had to leave right after the show.<BR>&gt;I also don't know who all the "main" members of the club are that they<BR>&gt;were refering to anyways. I said that I assumed you guys had impartial<BR>&gt;unbiased people doing the ballot counting and not any "main" members,<BR>&gt;especially ones who had Fieros in the show. Am I right?<BR>&gt;3) The third one came up last year after the Rutland show also, and that<BR>&gt;is: Why does it seem that the class(s) that Tim has his Fieros in always<BR>&gt;have more than three trophy's? My response to that was that your Fiero is<BR>&gt;an 88, and due to the large turn out in the 88 class, it would be easy to<BR>&gt;surmize an extra trophy for it. It was then pointed out to me that last<BR>&gt;year, the 87 year had more models than the 88's, but the 87 class didn't<BR>&gt;have 4 trophy's. I don't remember if that's the case nor do they mention<BR>&gt;which show they are refering to so I told them I couldn't comment on that<BR>&gt;statement either. Interesting question, but not one I have enough info on<BR>&gt;nor do I feel that it is my place to comment on or feel comfortable in<BR>&gt;doing so.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;All in all, I thought the show was pretty cool with the large turnout. I<BR>&gt;hope that these little grumblings don't launch anyone into a bad mode, as<BR>&gt;it seems to be just grumblings at this point anyway.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;Lastly, I was signed up within the time period to receive a T-Top poster.<BR>&gt;Is that being shipped to me?<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;Well, got to go back to work.<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;Steve<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;BTW: When is the next FOCONE newsletter due?<BR>&gt;<BR>&gt;||||reg||8
Z||000028||Chris Schaefer||06-20-2001||07:33 AM||||Steve,<P>Remember when you and your wife, mostly your wife, bad mouthed another Fiero group in New England?  Wasn't it NEFA?<P>Or how about when you asked me to help you with a membership problem with FOCOA?<P>I said that I would be glad to help but I would need to see a reciept for your money order that you sent them.  You told me, after dancing around the question, that you didn't have a reciept.  VERY INTERESTING.<P>So it is clear that you are not happy with anything or anyone.<P>BTW, the magazine I said you could have, after you picked it up, was to be given to new members when they signed up.  I should be sending you a bill for that book since you already received every issue that has been printed for this year so far.  The next issue is due, on schedule, the last week of July to the first week of August.<P>Chris<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000029||Boomtastic||06-20-2001||08:08 AM||||Well, I was going to ask how things went, but I'll refrain.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Congrats to all the winners!||||reg||1
Z||000030||Elvira||06-20-2001||09:55 AM||||Hey Eric,<BR>   Rob and Robbie had a great time!  I wish I could have gone but we had a houseful of people as you know.  Rob said Tim's t-top Fiero is beautiful!  He is on cloud 9 for taking second place (of course Josh is holding the trophy hostage until we bring the car down there :-)  He took a bunch of pics also.  Congrats to all the winners!<BR>             <P>------------------<BR>Elvira<P>Black 86GT 5sp x 2<BR>86SC t-top 58k miles||||reg||1
Z||000031||Fiero5||06-20-2001||11:52 AM||||Well, since I keep being misquoted, quoted out of context and some things just plain being made up out of the air, I will let this bickering now hopefully die a well deserved death.<BR>Those who know me and my family know how we are, and those who don't have had interesting things stated here, of which I have factually picked apart and shown how incorrect they are.<P>I think just about everyone on the forum here knows how the FOCOA thing went, as many, many others have also stepped up and stated similar experiences of not receieving what they paid for. Chris, I e-mailed you a scan of the receipt many months ago, and I heard nothing.<BR>Must be a problem with your ISP? Funny how you can always get an e-mail thru to me when you want to.<P>As for your trying to start some riff again with NEFA, give me break! Everyone there knows how that went and it was no big deal.<P>The Kelley Family had a great time at the OOB show. I am sorry that a few simple questions arose that could have easily and quickly been answered, but unforyunately exploded as many feared it would. Well, you live and learn I guess.<P>Now, let's let this part of the thread die and let's move on and see some more pics. This is unfortunatley taking away from the large number of awesome Fieros that were in attendance that day. Maybe start a new thread (which I will be more than happy to start with our many pics) so everyone doesn't have to scan thru all of this everytime to see any of them.<P>Sincerely,<P>Steve Kelley<BR>||||reg||9
Z||000032||Chris Schaefer||06-20-2001||01:16 PM||||Steve,<P>I read every posting and every reply with regards to you NEFA issue.  I thought that it was all in bad taste.  Slamming one car club and praising another in that fashion is in very poor taste.<P>As for the scanned receipt you E-mailed me, if you had sent me something and you did not hear from me why didn't you call me?<P>I even remember that your E-mail wasn't working properly for some time.  Mine was working fine.<P>I gave you my phone number back then.  <P>You should have call me.  But like I said, you danced around the question and then told me that you didn't have a receipt.  I remember it very vividly.  If I had seen something from you I would have done everything possible to have helped you.  I never received any scanned photo of your receipt so that is why I couldn't help you.  Something that I never told you, I called and talked to Gloria about your problem.  She told me straight out that she had no records of ever receiving anything from you.  So with out a receipt nothing could be done.  So it is rather hard to believe in something that can't be seen.  By this time it has been way over 1 year ago so I don't think there is anything left to do.<P>The only other thing that is possible is the same thing that happened to Rob D.  He mailed a membership payment to FOCONE, I believe April 2000.  Tim received a rather old envelope with a postmark from the time it was mailed almost exactly 1 year after it was mailed.  I couldn't believe it either until I saw the envelope myself.<P>Perhaps your letter/money order is lost and may yet turn up.  At the very least, you could take your money order receipt back to the post office and get your money back.  Which means that you would have been out nothing.  Right?<P>As for the whole OOB weekend thing, if you would like I could copy more communications that you sent to focone@focone.org to this list.  I know we all tried our best to answer your questions.  We even asked you to forward any E-mails you had with questions to us so we may properly address them to the proper people.<P>We haven't seen anything yet so we all consider this matter closed.<P>Look now I am late returning to work again.<BR>I have to go.<P>Chris<P>BTW, From everyone that I talked to at the show in OOB this past weekend, everyone had a really good time.  Our Rutland show this September 23, 2001 is sure to be even better.  We will have some new car classes so we can better match everyone together.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Chris Schaefer (edited 06-20-2001).]||||reg||9
Z||000033||chester||06-20-2001||01:55 PM||||Wow,<P>Nothing like stiring up a S**T storm.  I have pics of most of the cars that were on display at the OOB show and will post them Friday when I get back from Maryland unless someone else beats me to it.  Now EVERYONE SHAKE HANDS AND PLAY NICE!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Rob D.||||reg||4
Z||000034||Fiero2||06-20-2001||03:30 PM||||Chris, Steven has done nothing wrong here other than originally try to communicate to Tim some simple questions that arose out of the show, to give Tim a chance to answer them quickly before they possibly got out of hand. Tim has even called us at our home, one as recently as a few days before this show to ask about some things that were going around like the banquet/trophy issue. Tim asked him to next time communicate anything like that to him to give him a chance to take care of them. Steve did that as you can see from "one" of the e-mails that you have since posted here. We all see what happened now as a result of his trying to be a nice guy. Go read the very first post Steve put on this thread again. How on earth do you get anything bad out of that post?<P>As for your cheap shots like the one saying that Steve has complained before about not winning at shows, that is utter crap and you know it. I don't like your adding little made up snippets into your posts here and there to try and paint Steve in a bad light. You should be ashamed of yourself!<BR>What part of Steve's statement that he has never ever complained about not winning are you having a hard time understanding?<P>As for the NEFA issue, once again it was me that sent out that e-mail, not Steve. If you or anyone else has an issue with it take it up with me. Don't try now and twist the e-mails that I sent out back then to again attempt to try and make Steve look bad. As for it being in bad taste, everyone I have talked to all laughed later and understood where I was coming from.<P>I have heard just about enough now (seems like I have said that before), of all this bashing of my husband who has done nothing wrong here. He has done so much for many in the Fiero community and also for his own family. He spends as much or more time on his family's Fieros as he does on his own. This is not a man who deserves to have this kind of stuff thrown at him. Enough is enough!<